From 06b29851973498c0b3879f9b5a196795e59d1806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:18:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Number recorded screens, URL bar view buttons, Save screen
 now

Screens are numbered, and the right panel follows the flow strip:
- Every card in the recording panel shows its number in the recording,
  the same number as its card in the flow strip and in the preview (1, 2,
  3; a loading card after screen 2 is 2.1). A page still saving shows the
  number it is about to get.
- The panel lists cards in the flow strip's order (state.screens), not
  the order captures started in. A page whose save was held back (phone
  still capturing, its row pointed at a newer frame) used to sit above a
  screen saved before it.
- A screen whose row was dropped while its take waited still gets a row,
  so the panel never misses a screen the strip shows.

The URL bar's view buttons change the stage:
- Desktop + mobile, Desktop and Mobile are View as from the recording
  panel: picking one switches the stage, and each follows the other. They
  show in every view, not only side by side.
- Manual sides stay for re-records whose desktop and phone links differ.

Refresh screen is now Save screen now:
- It saves the card exactly as both sides look at that moment, whatever
  it was waiting on. Waiting on its phone: the phone is snapped as it is
  (and the desktop again, if it is still on that page), instead of
  sending the card back to "Saving..." behind the same wait. Held behind
  an earlier card: that card is saved first, then this one. Still
  settling: both sides are snapped now.
- Later frames of the page (fills, reloads, a second load) don't write
  over a screen saved this way.
- The phone job the snap cancels is closed, so the next page doesn't
  wait out the 45 s stall timer.
- A row for a page the desktop has left, with nothing of it taken, is
  dropped when the next document starts, instead of reading "Saving..."
  forever. Save screen now on such a row says the page isn't open.

